x})$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}."] [17592186311603 :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-x+5,$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(4{x}^{2}-x+5)$\n\n$$\n\\text{L2}:\\,\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{2}-x}{5}\\right)=0\n$$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,4{x}^{2}-x=O(5)$  as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5)$  as $x\\to 0$   \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  as $x\\to 0$ \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}."] [17592186311761 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\,\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{5{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11}{4{x}^{3}-4}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186311762 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-4x}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186311763 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{x}^{2}+3x}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186311764 :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }(4{x}^{13})=${{field-1}}"] [17592186311765 :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty }(-6{x}^{7})=${{field-1}}"] [17592186311766 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,\\lim_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-5)^{2}-48x+128}{{x}^{2}-6x+9}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186311767 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186311768 :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,\\lim_{x\